573:
(a) The following shall constitute nuisances and shall be unlawful:
(1) Any building, fence, billboard, or other structure on private property which abuts or fronts upon any public street or sidewalk and which is dilapidated or presents a threat to the public health, safety and/or welfare. "Dilapidated" shall mean in decay or a state of ruin.
(2) Any dwelling house, building, fence, billboard, or other structure on private property which abuts or fronts upon any public street or sidewalk and which, on the exterior of the structure, exhibits one (1) or more of the following conditions:
a. Broken windows;
b. Graffiti;
c. Loose or missing roof shingles;
d. Loose or missing window shutters;
e. Missing bricks or aluminum or vinyl siding;
f. Peeling paint; or
g. Any other exterior feature in a dilapidated condition.
(3) Any tree or other natural growth on any private property that is in danger of falling and creates a substantial risk of damage or injury.
(4) Any ivy, kudzu or other vine on any private property that encroaches upon neighboring property.
(5) Any tarp, plastic sheeting, or other temporary covering on any dwelling house, building, fence, billboard, or other structure for a period of greater than ten (10) days. This section shall not apply to any tarp, plastic sheeting, or other temporary covering used during the process of construction or repair of any structure.
(Ord. No. 2000-14, § 1, 6-19-00)

589:
(a) Noise generated from municipally sponsored or approved celebrations or events shall be exempt from the provisions of this article.
